25,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems general-purpose spaces are in high demand, while specialist ones sit idle. Also, shared booking spaces are rated much higher by users.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that matches my findings on booking data. However, I found that taking rooms out of service requires expensive off-site hiring.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I've noticed a pattern: comfort-based projects always slip by a year, and outdoor work is heavily delayed by weather.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The costs are drifting! Mechanical plant prices are rising fast, and we have no money set aside to replace old AV equipment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks because the equipment is outdated, yet we have unfilled grounds and front-of-house posts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, if the equipment is failing the staff, that's a priority. But we must ensure the result is a space people actually use.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if outdoor work is risky for the schedule, we should be cautious about any plan involving external paths.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. A project that slips a year is a failure of planning. We need something predictable and high-impact.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are spiking, a big ventilation project might blow the budget. We need to be careful.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the current manual routines are a drain on staff. It's not just about the budget; it's about the labor.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, if off-site hiring is expensive, a conversion of an existing underused hall might be the most efficient path.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Victoria,,That would minimize the disruption to the timetable compared to a full laboratory overhaul.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,A ground-floor conversion is likely more stable than outdoor work or complex mechanical installations.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about the AV costs for a new center, but a study commons seems manageable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I still think the lab staff need relief, but I see the logic regarding the budget and schedule.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,Let's see the candidates and decide based on these risks and needs.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Victoria,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Kenji,,Let's do it!,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Fine by me.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
